    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test class \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 the only one in the project).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe feature: when a `POST /api/owners` request includes `birthDate` (ISO), the owner's `ageBand` is derived (`MINOR` <18, `ADULT` 18\u201364, `SENIOR` 65+) against its `registrationDate` and returned on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nThe app maps requests/responses through OpenAPI-generated DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`) via MapStruct, which maps by property name, and the persisted `Owner` entity is loaded from a fixed `schema.sql` (`ddl-auto=none` under the test's `hsqldb` profile). So four coordinated edits were needed:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (`format: date`) to the editable `OwnerFields` schema, and `ageBand` (readOnly string) to the `Owner` response schema. Kept `ageBand` a plain string (not an enum) to match the existing computed string fields like `contactPreference`/`locality`, so MapStruct maps it identically.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with accessors, and a computed `getAgeBand()` that returns the band from complete years between `birthDate` and `registrationDate` (falling back to today only if the registration date isn't set yet), or `null` when no birth date is present. Like the other derived getters (`membershipNumber`, `initials`), it has no setter, so MapStruct treats it as read-only output.\n\n3. **`schema.sql`** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added a `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table so the entity's new field persists and reads back.\n\nMapStruct then auto-maps `birthDate` in on create and `ageBand` out on read. The acceptance test (`birthDate` 1990-01-01 \u2192 `ADULT` against today, 2026-09-03 \u2192 age 36) passes.",
